window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-3b803d2803176fe7"]={"key":"ny_b1-3b803d2803176fe7","group":"ny_b1","uid":"3b803d2803176fe7","rank":15,"title":"qapi executive summary transition compliance","occupation":"registered_nurses","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You are Sofia Sepulveda, the RN quality lead for Goldfinch Alliance, preparing material for Bekele Underwood before the governing body meeting in November. Our annual QAPI report, goldfinch_qapi_annual_report.docx, runs to 190 pages across four service lines, and Bekele will read only a short executive summary before the meeting. Prepare goldfinch_qapi_executive_summary.docx in exactly two pages and qapi_measure_table.xlsx as the matching one-slide measure table; write both files into the top level of the working directory using exactly those filenames. The summary must tell the governing body what it needs to decide this year, while still giving a fair picture of the four service lines. The vascular-access infection trend is buried deep in the report and appears to be the only matter that calls for a governing-body decision, so do not let the many well-performing measures crowd it out, but do not turn a reported concern into a finding that the source does not support. One of Goldfinch Alliance's contracted service lines is delivered with Ravensmoor Manufacturing, and its practice is partway through a change: the current-period process and the intended end-state process overlap during the reporting window. Make the timing and status of measures clear enough that a trustee can tell what is current, what is transitional, and what is not yet in force. Draw a defensible line between binding compliance requirements and desirable improvement language in this setting, and be precise about what the evidence does and does not establish. Present facts and the decision context without recommending an action or taking one on the board's behalf. Keep patient, resident, and employee information to the minimum necessary for governance review, use the report's terminology and figures consistently, and do not invent figures, causes, thresholds, commitments, or legal conclusions. The two files must agree wherever they show the same measure, period, denominator, status, or figure, and the spreadsheet must be usable as a single projected slide rather than as a data dump.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/goldfinch_qapi_annual_report.docx` — The complete annual QAPI report from which the executive summary and measure table must be prepared.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `goldfinch_qapi_executive_summary.docx` — A two-page executive summary for governing-body review. (Exactly two rendered pages.; Written for trustees and a peer quality reviewer, not as a restatement of the full report.; Must present facts and decision context without recommending or taking action.; Must distinguish current-period, transitional, and end-state status.; Must minimize sensitive information and avoid unsupported causal, legal, or compliance claims.)\n- `qapi_measure_table.xlsx` — A matching one-slide measure table containing the executive-level measures and figures. (Must be formatted to project as one readable slide/page.; Must use the same measure names, periods, denominators, statuses, and figures as the executive summary.; Must not add unsupported measures or figures.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/goldfinch_qapi_annual_report.docx","bytes":38604,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/b2b70864c77f0918ea3d496ac027b3e22daf8766ee26a0f0a41d5f333c409c02.docx","sha256":"b2b70864c77f0918ea3d496ac027b3e22daf8766ee26a0f0a41d5f333c409c02","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Goldfinch Alliance\nAnnual QAPI Report | FY2025\nPrepared for internal quality and governing-body review | Reporting year: January 1–December 31, 2025\nScope and evidence note\nThis report aggregates service-line quality measures for governance review. Percentages and rates retain their source denominators. Narrative findings are descriptive; the report does not establish causation, legal noncompliance, or a contractual breach unless expressly stated.\nService-line index\n1. Home Health\n2. Hospice\n3. Ravensmoor Manufacturing Occupational Health (contracted service line)\n4. Vascular Access Services\n\n\n1. Home Health\nMeasure: Medication reconciliation completed within 48 hours of start of care. FY2025: 98 of 100 eligible starts (98%). FY2024 comparison: 96 of 100 (96%). Status: Stable, with the current-period result higher than the prior comparison period. The denominator is eligible starts of care; no patient-level identifiers are included.\nOperational note: This measure describes completion documentation and does not, by itself, establish medication safety outcomes.\n2. Hospice\nMeasure: Comprehensive symptom reassessment documented within 48 hours after an urgent symptom call. FY2025: 47 of 50 urgent calls (94%). FY2024 comparison: 45 of 50 (90%). Status: Improving. The denominator is urgent symptom calls meeting the report definition.\nOperational note: The measure is a documentation-timeliness percentage, not a claim about symptom relief.\n\n\n3. Ravensmoor Manufacturing Occupational Health\nContracted service line. Measure: Exposure follow-up documentation completed within two business days. Current-period process (in force January 1–October 31, 2025): paper log entry plus supervisor sign-off; 18 of 20 eligible exposure follow-ups (90%) met the two-business-day interval. Status for that period: Current process / 90%.\nTransition window: November 1–December 31, 2025. Ravensmoor and Goldfinch began using the electronic attestation workflow alongside the paper log. Evidence for the overlap is incomplete in the annual report; the two processes should not be combined into one result. Intended end-state process: electronic attestation at the time of follow-up, effective January 1, 2026, subject to completion of the implementation condition recorded in the contract appendix. End-state status at December 31, 2025: Not yet in force.\nApplicability boundary: The current-period process is the process against which FY2025 documentation is described. The end-state workflow is a defined future-state improvement and is not treated here as a current-period compliance requirement.\n4. Vascular Access Services\nMeasure: Vascular-access infection events per 1,000 line-days. Numerator: infection events meeting the report definition; denominator: central-line days. Quarterly trend: Q1 2025, 0/1,260 = 0.00 per 1,000 line-days; Q2, 1/1,290 = 0.78; Q3, 1/1,310 = 0.76; Q4, 3/1,240 = 2.42. FY2024 comparison: 2/5,180 = 0.39 per 1,000 line-days. Status: Concerning trend in Q4; the annual report does not set a regulatory threshold.\nEvidence boundary: The report notes a temporal association between the Q4 increase and a supply change under review. The data do not establish that the supply change caused the infections, and they do not establish a legal, regulatory, or contractual finding.\nGovernance relevance: This is the only measure in the annual report identified for governing-body decision context because the Q4 rate is above each preceding quarter and above the FY2024 comparison rate. The report presents the trend and evidence limits for trustee consideration; it does not recommend a response.\n\n\nAppendix: measure definitions and status language\nStatus labels are descriptive: Stable means the current result is consistent with the prior comparison; Improving means the current result is higher than the prior comparison for a completion percentage; Current process identifies the process in force during the reported period; Transitional identifies overlap with incomplete evidence; Not yet in force identifies the intended end state after the reporting window; Concerning trend identifies a direction requiring governance attention without asserting a breach.\nSource basis: Goldfinch Alliance Annual QAPI Report, FY2025, aggregate service-line tables and transition appendix. Prepared by Sofia Sepulveda, RN Quality Lead, for Bekele Underwood and governing-body review in November.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/goldfinch_qapi_executive_summary.docx","bytes":39168,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/aaae371a892a1f50710284ebecae84ac903b2f53f4e832084edc9213e3ecaef7.docx","sha256":"aaae371a892a1f50710284ebecae84ac903b2f53f4e832084edc9213e3ecaef7","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"GOLDFINCH ALLIANCE\nExecutive QAPI Summary | FY2025\nFor Bekele Underwood and governing-body review | November meeting | Prepared by Sofia Sepulveda, RN Quality Lead\nDecision issue at a glance\nVascular-access infection events increased in Q4 2025 to 3 events over 1,240 central-line days (2.42 per 1,000 line-days), after 0.00 in Q1, 0.78 in Q2, and 0.76 in Q3. The FY2024 comparison was 2/5,180 (0.39 per 1,000 line-days). This is the only measure the annual report identifies for governing-body decision context. The figures show a concerning trend; they do not establish a cause, threshold breach, or legal or contractual finding.\nExecutive measure snapshot\nService line / measure\nPeriod\nPopulation / denominator\nResult\nStatus\nHome Health — medication reconciliation within 48 hours\nFY2025 (FY2024 comparison)\n100 eligible starts (prior 100)\n98/100 = 98% (prior 96%)\nStable\nHospice — symptom reassessment within 48 hours of urgent call\nFY2025 (FY2024 comparison)\n50 urgent calls (prior 50)\n47/50 = 94% (prior 90%)\nImproving\nRavensmoor Manufacturing Occupational Health — exposure follow-up within 2 business days\nJan–Oct 2025 current process\n20 eligible follow-ups\n18/20 = 90%\nCurrent process\nVascular Access Services — infection events per 1,000 line-days\nQ4 2025 (Q1–Q3 trend; FY2024 comparison)\n1,240 central-line days (FY2024: 5,180)\n3/1,240 = 2.42 per 1,000 (FY2024: 0.39)\nConcerning trend\nInterpretive frame\nThe four lines are represented proportionately: Home Health is stable, Hospice is improving, Ravensmoor is measured against the process in force during the period, and Vascular Access is the sole concerning trend. Percentages and rates retain their source denominators; event counts are not presented as rates, and rates are not presented as compliance percentages.\nSource: Goldfinch Alliance Annual QAPI Report, FY2025, service-line tables and transition appendix. Aggregate data only.\n\n\nSTATUS, TRANSITION, AND EVIDENCE BOUNDARIES\nRavensmoor Manufacturing contracted practice\nCurrent-period process (in force January 1–October 31, 2025): paper log entry plus supervisor sign-off. Eighteen of 20 eligible exposure follow-ups (90%) met the two-business-day interval. During the November 1–December 31 transition window, the electronic attestation workflow ran alongside the paper log; overlap evidence is incomplete and is not combined with the 90% result. The intended end-state process is electronic attestation at the time of follow-up, effective January 1, 2026, subject to the implementation condition in the contract appendix. At December 31, 2025 it was not yet in force.\nCompliance versus improvement language\nFor FY2025, the applicable/current process is the paper-log workflow described above. The electronic workflow is a defined future-state improvement, not a current-period compliance requirement, and its absence in FY2025 is not characterized as a failure. “Must” is reserved for a requirement that is applicable and effective in the source; “should” describes a desirable improvement or an end state not yet effective. The annual report supplies no jurisdiction-specific threshold for the vascular-access rate.\nVascular-access decision context\nQuarterly rate sequence: Q1 0/1,260 = 0.00; Q2 1/1,290 = 0.78; Q3 1/1,310 = 0.76; Q4 3/1,240 = 2.42 per 1,000 central-line days. The Q4 result is above each preceding quarter and the FY2024 comparison (2/5,180 = 0.39), which is why it merits governing-body attention relative to the other measures. The report notes a temporal association with a supply change under review; the evidence does not prove causation or identify a patient outcome.\nWhat is before the governing body\nTrustees are presented with the vascular-access trend, its denominators, and the evidence limits for decision consideration. The summary records the issue and status distinctions without recommending an action, setting a new threshold, or making a legal, regulatory, or contractual conclusion.\nSource basis: Goldfinch Alliance Annual QAPI Report, FY2025. Prepared for November governing-body review.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/private/gold/qapi_measure_table.xlsx","bytes":6390,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/4af060fb036576cf9c001501ace2684dac47c7daa772c426dec1be15356eee6c.xlsx","sha256":"4af060fb036576cf9c001501ace2684dac47c7daa772c426dec1be15356eee6c","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Executive Measures","row_count":8,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["GOLDFINCH ALLIANCE | FY2025 EXECUTIVE QAPI MEASURES"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Governing-body view | Aggregate results; source: Annual QAPI Report FY2025"]},{"r":"4","cells":["Service line / measure","Period and comparison","Population / denominator","Result","Status","Evidence / timing note"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Home Health — medication reconciliation within 48 hours","FY2025; FY2024 comparison","100 eligible starts; prior 100","98/100 = 98%; prior 96%","Stable","Completion documentation measure"]},{"r":"6","cells":["Hospice — symptom reassessment within 48 hours of urgent call","FY2025; FY2024 comparison","50 urgent calls; prior 50","47/50 = 94%; prior 90%","Improving","Timeliness percentage; not symptom outcome"]},{"r":"7","cells":["Ravensmoor Manufacturing Occupational Health — exposure follow-up within 2 business days","Jan–Oct 2025 current process","20 eligible follow-ups","18/20 = 90%","Current process","Paper log + supervisor sign-off; Nov–Dec overlap incomplete"]},{"r":"8","cells":["Vascular Access Services — infection events per 1,000 line-days","Q4 2025; Q1–Q3 trend; FY2024 comparison","1,240 central-line days; FY2024 5,180","3/1,240 = 2.42 per 1,000; FY2024 0.39","Concerning trend","Q1 0.00; Q2 0.78; Q3 0.76; no threshold stated"]},{"r":"10","cells":["Status key: Stable / Improving = current-period comparison; Current process = process in force; Concerning trend = governance attention without a source-defined threshold. End-state electronic attestation for Ravensmoor effective Jan 1, 2026; not yet in force at Dec 31, 2025."]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submission contains goldfinch_qapi_executive_summary.docx.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Submitted working-directory files.","grader_hint":"Check exact filename and readable DOCX structure."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submission contains qapi_measure_table.xlsx.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Submitted working-directory files.","grader_hint":"Check exact filename and readable XLSX structure."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The rendered executive summary is exactly two pages.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Rendered DOCX pagination.","grader_hint":"Render with a standard office engine and count pages; do not infer from the document's page-number text."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The measure table is configured and rendered as one readable projected page or slide rather than a multi-page worksheet.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Rendered XLSX print area, scaling, and visual output.","grader_hint":"Inspect print settings and render; accept a single coherent projection-oriented table."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The summary identifies Goldfinch Alliance and the governing-body audience and uses an executive-level framing.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Summary title and opening text.","grader_hint":"Look for organization, audience, reporting purpose, and concise executive framing."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The summary gives each of the four service lines a proportionate, evidence-based status rather than omitting or inventing a service line.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Service-line coverage compared with the four service lines in the supplied report.","grader_hint":"Verify all four source service lines appear and are represented without equal-space treatment being required."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The summary identifies the vascular-access infection trend as the report's governing-body decision issue and explains why it merits attention relative to the other measures.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Summary discussion compared with the vascular-access section and board-relevance evidence in the source.","grader_hint":"Credit a clear prioritization tied to trend and governance relevance, not merely a mention of the measure."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The summary states the vascular-access measure's reporting period, numerator, denominator, and calculated rate or equivalent source-defined figure accurately.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source measure definition and reported values.","grader_hint":"Recalculate where applicable and compare all four components with the source."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The summary describes the vascular-access trend across the relevant comparison periods accurately and does not collapse distinct periods into one claim.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source trend table or narrative and summary trend statement.","grader_hint":"Check direction, sequence, and period labels against the source."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The summary distinguishes an observed association or trend from a proven cause and does not state that a named intervention caused the infection result unless the source establishes causation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Summary language and source evidentiary wording.","grader_hint":"Credit cautious evidence language; reject causal assertions unsupported by the report."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The summary explains what the governing body is being asked to decide without converting that decision context into a recommendation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Decision-context wording in the summary.","grader_hint":"Look for a clearly bounded decision or issue presented neutrally, with no preferred option, instruction, or commitment by the author."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"A trustee can identify the single principal decision issue quickly without reading the full report.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered summary as a whole.","grader_hint":"Judge hierarchy, prominence, and clarity, not merely the presence of the words 'decision' or 'board'."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The summary describes the contracted practice involving Ravensmoor Manufacturing only to the extent supported by the source and identifies its operational relevance.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source contract/service-line material and summary.","grader_hint":"Check correct attribution and relevance; do not reward invented organizational roles or obligations."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The summary explicitly distinguishes the process that governed the current reporting period from the intended end-state process.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source transition notes and summary status language.","grader_hint":"Require separate current and future/end-state descriptions, not a single blended process statement."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The summary identifies the transition timing or effective-status boundary sufficiently for a reader to know what was in force during the reported period.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Effective dates and transition statements in the source.","grader_hint":"Compare dates and status qualifiers with the source; accept an equivalent precise timeline."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The summary draws an explicit and defensible distinction between requirements that are binding in the source and practices that are desirable improvements.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source wording, effective-status material, and summary modality.","grader_hint":"Look for a clear must/should or equivalent boundary grounded in applicability and status, not casual synonym use."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The summary does not present a future-state practice as a current compliance failure when the source shows that the future state was not yet effective.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source effective-status evidence and summary conclusions.","grader_hint":"Assess both the statement and its temporal qualifier."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The summary states the status of each executive-level measure using labels that agree with the source evidence and definitions.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Summary status labels compared with source results.","grader_hint":"Check that compliant, improving, stable, concerning, transitional, or equivalent labels are not contradicted by the underlying data."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The summary includes the source-defined denominator or population context wherever a rate, percentage, or compliance statement could otherwise be misleading.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Measure definitions and summary text/table.","grader_hint":"Require enough population context to interpret each prominent quantitative claim."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The summary preserves the source's distinction between event counts, rates, and compliance percentages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source measures and summary expressions.","grader_hint":"Reject conversions or labels that change the measure type."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The summary identifies the reporting period and comparison basis for each prominently reported measure.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source period definitions and summary.","grader_hint":"Check both current period and comparison period where the source uses one."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"All figures used in the summary are traceable to the supplied report, with calculations either source-supported or transparently derived from source values.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Every quantitative statement and its source counterpart.","grader_hint":"Audit figures, percentages, trend claims, and derived rates; do not require formal footnotes if traceability is otherwise clear."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The summary does not assert a legal conclusion, regulatory finding, patient outcome, or contractual breach that the supplied report does not establish.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Summary claims compared with source authority.","grader_hint":"Apply a doctrinal evidence-boundary review; distinguish reporting a source statement from independently asserting a stronger conclusion."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The summary states limitations or uncertainty where the source itself qualifies the evidence, rather than presenting qualified evidence as definitive.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Qualified source passages and summary wording.","grader_hint":"Look for preserved qualifiers, scope limits, and uncertainty."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The summary uses the source's measure names and operational definitions consistently enough that a peer reviewer can map each claim back to the report.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source headings/definitions and summary terminology.","grader_hint":"Allow minor plain-language glosses when the source term remains identifiable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The summary handles sensitive information minimally and contains no unnecessary patient, resident, employee, or individual-level identifiers.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered summary and table.","grader_hint":"Check for aggregation and removal of unnecessary names, dates of birth, record numbers, or case details."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The summary is usable by a governing-body reader without requiring the author to explain abbreviations, measure scope, or status terminology.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered summary.","grader_hint":"Judge plain-language expansion of essential abbreviations and local terms."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The summary makes the important vascular-access issue prominent while giving lower-risk, well-performing measures concise but non-misleading coverage.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered two-page hierarchy.","grader_hint":"Assess prioritization and proportionality visually and substantively."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The summary ends on the decision or governing-body issue rather than on an unrequested next-steps list or an authorial recommendation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Final paragraph or concluding section of the summary.","grader_hint":"Inspect the ending for neutral decision framing and absence of action plan prose."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The measure table includes the same executive-level measures selected in the summary and no material measure presented in one deliverable is absent from the other.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Both deliverables and source measure list.","grader_hint":"Compare measure identities, not row order or styling."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every figure shared by the summary and measure table agrees exactly in value and unit, subject to equivalent formatting such as decimal or percent display.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-document figure audit.","grader_hint":"Compare counts, rates, percentages, denominators, and dates; allow only display-format equivalence."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Shared measure periods and comparison labels agree across the summary and measure table.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-document period labels.","grader_hint":"Check current, prior, transitional, and end-state labels wherever repeated."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Shared measure statuses agree across the summary and measure table, including the distinction between current and end-state status.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-document status labels and qualifiers.","grader_hint":"Do not accept a neutral table label that contradicts a qualified summary conclusion."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The table provides enough column context to identify the measure, period, population or denominator, result, and status without consulting the summary.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered spreadsheet table.","grader_hint":"Judge whether a single slide remains interpretable on its own."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The projected table is legible at slide scale, with no material clipping, hidden columns, unreadable text, or excessive empty structure.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered XLSX output.","grader_hint":"Render at fit-to-page or equivalent and judge practical readability."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The table does not imply that a source-defined future or desirable state is already achieved.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Table status and timing labels compared with source.","grader_hint":"Inspect labels, color keys, footnotes, and captions for temporal overstatement."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The summary and table identify the source or reporting basis sufficiently for a reviewer to verify the figures without a second factual attachment.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Source note, report reference, or equivalent traceability in both deliverables.","grader_hint":"Accept a concise source citation or report-period note that points unambiguously to the supplied report."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Neither deliverable contains invented thresholds, targets, causes, commitments, board decisions, or obligations not supported by the supplied report.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Complete content audit against the source.","grader_hint":"Credit evidence discipline; distinguish harmless connective prose from new factual assertions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The two deliverables together provide a coherent compliance assessment rather than a generic QAPI overview or a copied report index.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Both rendered deliverables as a package.","grader_hint":"Judge whether selection, status, evidence boundaries, and transition treatment demonstrate RN quality-review judgment."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The language is specific and unambiguous about what is observed, what is required, what is recommended by the source if anything, and what remains for governing-body consideration.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Summary and table wording.","grader_hint":"Review modality, qualifiers, and labels; vague verbs or blended obligation language should not receive full credit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The deliverables do not contain an authorial recommendation or an instruction that purports to decide or implement the governing body's action.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Both deliverables.","grader_hint":"This is a positive evidence-boundary criterion: neutral presentation is required, not an explicit disclaimer."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX and XLSX open and render without corruption, broken formulas, missing content, or materially altered values.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Office-library validation and rendered outputs.","grader_hint":"Open both files with standard offline office tooling; inspect formulas or cached values where used."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"An RN quality lead is condensing a multi-service-line QAPI record for governing-body review while a contracted practice is moving from a current process to a defined end state. The work is a compliance-oriented communication product: it must preserve evidentiary boundaries and status distinctions while remaining useful under a severe space constraint.","difficulty_sources":["Severe compression of a four-service-line QAPI report into a fixed two-page governance document.","Need to prioritize the one actionable vascular-access trend without overstating its evidence.","Need to distinguish current, transitional, and end-state practice status.","Need to draw a defensible must/should boundary and preserve doctrinal evidence limits.","Need to keep an executive summary and a one-slide measure table numerically and semantically aligned."],"authoring_plan":{"source_construction":{"filename":"goldfinch_qapi_annual_report.docx","purpose":"Create one internally consistent, offline-readable annual QAPI report for Goldfinch Alliance covering four service lines, including a contracted service line involving Ravensmoor Manufacturing.","content_constraints":["Include stable service-line names, measure definitions, reporting periods, denominators, numerators, rates, comparison values, status descriptions, and source language for all executive-level measures.","Make the vascular-access infection measure the only measure with a governing-body decision implication, supported by a clearly visible trend and relevant context buried later in the report.","Include several well-performing measures that deserve brief coverage but no governing-body decision.","Include a practice transition affecting the Ravensmoor Manufacturing service line: define the current-period process, the transition window, the effective date or condition for the end-state process, and the evidence status during the overlap.","Use source language that permits a competent reviewer to distinguish binding requirements from desirable improvements without relying on jurisdiction-specific law.","Include enough qualified wording to test that the solver does not convert association into causation, a future state into current noncompliance, or a reported issue into a legal or contractual finding.","Use aggregate data only; include no real or unnecessary individual identifiers."]},"gold_derivation":{"method":"Build a reference summary and table from the source using source-defined measures and calculations, then audit every figure and status across the two deliverables.","required_reasoning":["Select the vascular-access infection trend as the central governance issue because it is the only source-supported issue requiring a board decision.","Represent the four service lines proportionately, giving concise status coverage to well-performing measures.","Separate current-period status, transition-period status, and end-state status.","Draw the must/should boundary from applicability, effective status, and source wording; do not import an external rule.","State what the evidence shows and does not show, including the absence of unsupported causal, legal, or contractual conclusions.","Present the board decision context neutrally and do not supply a recommendation."],"cross_file_invariants":["The same measure names, periods, denominators, results, units, and statuses must appear consistently wherever repeated.","The central vascular-access figure and trend must agree in both files.","The transition and end-state labels must not imply that the future state was already effective.","The table must contain only measures selected for the executive summary."]}},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"primary_plus_appendix","structure":"strict_schema"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"qapi_annual_report","filename":"goldfinch_qapi_annual_report.docx","purpose":"The complete annual QAPI report from which the executive summary and measure table must be prepared.","required":true,"discovery":"Use this supplied Word document as the sole factual source; its service-line sections, measure definitions, reporting periods, transition notes, and appendices contain the evidence needed for the deliverables."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"executive_summary","filename":"goldfinch_qapi_executive_summary.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A two-page executive summary for governing-body review.","required":true,"constraints":["Exactly two rendered pages.","Written for trustees and a peer quality reviewer, not as a restatement of the full report.","Must present facts and decision context without recommending or taking action.","Must distinguish current-period, transitional, and end-state status.","Must minimize sensitive information and avoid unsupported causal, legal, or compliance claims."],"rendering_required":true},{"deliverable_id":"measure_table","filename":"qapi_measure_table.xlsx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet","description":"A matching one-slide measure table containing the executive-level measures and figures.","required":true,"constraints":["Must be formatted to project as one readable slide/page.","Must use the same measure names, periods, denominators, statuses, and figures as the executive summary.","Must not add unsupported measures or figures."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"document_information","work_product":"compliance_assessment","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"registered_nurses","sector":"healthcare_social_assistance","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":3.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"Have a domain-expert reviewer assess clinical-quality evidence boundaries, transition status, and governance usefulness, and have an independent reviewer verify figures, cross-deliverable agreement, pagination, and rendering.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["Judgments about executive prominence and projected readability require rendered visual review.","The source uses an intentionally bounded internal transition context rather than a jurisdiction-specific regulatory framework, so reviewers should not import external legal requirements."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:43:01+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:43:01+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:43:01+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:43:01+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:43:01+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/3b803d2803176fe7","declared_deliverables":["goldfinch_qapi_executive_summary.docx","qapi_measure_table.xlsx"]};
